Rule 1 (out tensor must have the same dtype as input to avoid cast errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor must match input tensor’s dimensionality and shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 3 (scalar handling: scalar input implies scalar out; otherwise shapes must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then ndim(v_2) = 0 else (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 4 (limit input magnitude to reduce risk of overflow to infinity on CPU implementations)
{v_1 : tensor} |= max(v_1) ≤ 20 ∧ min(v_1) ≥ -20
